Your final paper will hinge on visual proofs showing exactly how the tokens move through your custom layers.

**The Routing Frequency Heatmap (`heatmap.py`)**
This script generates a 2D map with the 7 Experts on the Y-axis and the 7 Recursion Steps on the X-axis. For 100 runs, it logs which expert was selected at each specific depth step. In your paper, a clean, defined path across this heatmap visually proves temporal composition—showing that a token smoothly transitions from one logical operation expert to the next as it gets deeper into the loop.

**The Hardness vs. Depth Correlation (`correlation.py`)**
This is the ultimate proof of adaptive compute. By plotting Average Execution Depth against dataset difficulty (Low Complexity vs. High Complexity), you should see a distinct "step-ladder pattern". Simple tokens exit early, while complex, nested logic utilizes the full loop, proving your primary efficiency thesis.

